Ahaaa... a polyless-wishless-genoless. This was
not definately planned, but since RGRN spared me
 from the worst, so to speak, I decided to go for it.

I got an amulet of reflection from sokoban, and shortly
afterwards a bag of holding from mines, on the floor.

I had collected a number of scrolls, and managed to identify
them around dlevel 9 (after completing the mines).
I reverse-geno'ed gray dragons and got scales.
Later I got a shield of reflection from an Aleax.

I got my 1st magic marker just before Castle, and
Frost Brand from mordor orc in second level of Gehennom.

Scary moments: mmfs were eating my brain constantly, luckily
I had memorized (in my real-life physical brain) the appearance of
a scroll of identify. But it took a while to re-discover scroll
of enchant armor, and I had almost mapped whole of Gehennom
before I could improve my AC from -21.

There were some scary moments in astral plane, particularly from
Pestilence, but nothing I could handle. Then again, I just might
could have wasted one "oLS, which would lower the style points :)

I found speed boots in the main dungeons, a hawaiian shirt and
an oilskin cloak in an armor store. I think I found a GoP at
Moloch's, but they were cursed and I had no scrolls of EA and
no magic markers left either.

I also used the Sceptre against disenchanters just too many times
in order to effectively use it, and since I got Frosty, I used
the Sceptre mostly for conflict.


